```javascript
function mergeArrays(arr1, arr2) {
  const map = new Map();

  // Helper function to add an object to the map
  const addToMap = (obj) => {
    const key = `${obj.stepId}-${obj.fieldId}`;
    if (map.has(key)) {
      const existing = map.get(key);
      if (existing.message && obj.message) {
        existing.message = `${existing.message};${obj.message}`;
      } else if (obj.message) {
        existing.message = obj.message;
      }
    } else {
      map.set(key, { ...obj });
    }
  };

  // Process both arrays
  arr1.forEach(addToMap);
  arr2.forEach(addToMap);

  return Array.from(map.values());
}
```

This function:
1. Creates a Map to store unique objects by a combined key of stepId and fieldId
2. Iterates through both arrays, adding each object to the map
3. If an object with the same stepId and fieldId already exists:
   - If both have messages, combines them with ';'
   - If only the new one has a message, uses that
   - If only the existing one has a message, keeps it
4. Returns the values of the map as an array

